    "title": "USDA opens disaster aid for 2023-2024 crop losses - NewsBreak",
    "text": "WICHITA, Kan. (KSNW) — Farmers who lost crops to drought, floods, or other natural disasters in 2023 and 2024 can now apply for federal disaster assistance. The U.S. Department of Agriculture announced Wednesday that $16 billion in aid is now available through the Supplemental Disaster Relief Program (SDRP). The first phase of the program opens July 10 and covers producers who already received crop insurance or NAP payments for their losses. Farmers should begin receiving pre-filled applications by mail this week. The USDA says producers can take those forms to their local Farm Service Agency office to apply. A second phase of the program—meant for losses not covered by insurance—will open later this fall. More details and tools are available at farmers.gov or through local USDA offices. For more Kansas news, click here . Keep up with the latest breaking news by downloading our mobile app and signing up for our news email alerts . Sign up for our Storm Track 3 Weather app by clicking here . To watch our shows live on our website, click here. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSN-TV.",
